WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.633
The six month execution plan.

2
00:00:02.933 --> 00:00:07.400
It runs alongside your study, and turns what you learn into projects you can show.

3
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.397
You are studying three hundred and eight topics.

4
00:00:11.397 --> 00:00:15.300
This plan is the project spine that turns that study into evidence.

5
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.867
Here is the whole plan.

6
00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:20.333
Months one and two: production RAG.

7
00:00:20.633 --> 00:00:23.168
Month three: agentic systems and MCP.

8
00:00:23.168 --> 00:00:26.867
This is the month that most changes your market value.

9
00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:29.433
Month four: fine-tuning and alignment.

10
00:00:29.733 --> 00:00:32.300
Month five: inference and cost engineering.

11
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:35.800
And month six: LLMOps and production hardening.

12
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.167
Every phase ends with something you ship.

13
00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:45.267
First, enterprise document Q and A, with a measured retrieval accuracy and citations.

14
00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:49.967
Then a multi-agent research assistant, judged with trajectory evals.

15
00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:54.567
Then a domain model that beats a frontier model on your own niche benchmark.

16
00:00:54.867 --> 00:00:59.233
And a serving stack with a before and after table of real latency and cost.

17
00:01:00.433 --> 00:01:03.533
Month six wraps a platform around everything you built.

18
00:01:03.833 --> 00:01:05.967
Your first three projects sit at the bottom.

19
00:01:06.267 --> 00:01:08.167
Tracing goes on top of all of them.

20
00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:11.333
Then guardrails and a CI and CD pipeline.

21
00:01:11.633 --> 00:01:15.700
And finally a cost dashboard, latency targets and drift detection.

22
00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.867
The last two months are about being seen.

23
00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:22.933
Clean up your repos, with READMEs, diagrams and benchmarks.

24
00:01:23.233 --> 00:01:29.033
Write four or five deep technical posts, and contribute to an open source project you really use.

25
00:01:29.333 --> 00:01:30.842
Post weekly on LinkedIn.

26
00:01:30.842 --> 00:01:33.167
Visibility compounds while you sleep.

27
00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:35.096
Let's recap.

28
00:01:35.096 --> 00:01:37.833
The plan is the project spine for your study.

29
00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:40.033
Each phase ships something measurable.

30
00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.367
Month six adds the platform layer.

31
00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:45.552
And the final months make your work public.

32
00:01:45.552 --> 00:01:47.700
Next up: five unfair advantages.
